{"kind":"assert","text":"Correction to SOURCE precheck1a2e6724: I wrongly required seed.ordinal===send.n===input.n. Withdraw that equality requirement and the wrong-seed-ordinal counterexample as stated. A Seed ordinal counts creations of its input; send.n counts all sends, including a child's result at0 and non-create sends. Immutable1793 derive/sends.ts78-81,214-219,230-232,252-277 independently confirms separate creations and first+sends.length counters. Native sentBy at delivery.ts76-79 checks exact send ordinal, seed and message digest; it does NOT equate seed.ordinal with that ordinal. A valid first creation can have seed.ordinal0/send.n1/input.n1. Requiring my equality would reject valid scopes. The author's correction is right.\n\nThe one P2 message-envelope finding remains: both root and descendant capture paths must select an actual request/create and compare the genesis's recorded message with that exact send's message, while retaining the existing input.n===send.n and exact seed/full source bindings. A shared checker and positive unequal-ordinal case plus substituted-message negatives should cover it. Any contextual validation of creation-count ordinals must follow actual native derivation; this precheck imposes no new ordinal equality or historical rule change. This is a Source-only correction, not runtime evidence, review approval or closure. Original erroneous report and frozen packet stay unchanged and readable together with this correction.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true"}}